Comment (internal/bench/evidence_ingest_benchmark_integration_test.go:214):
**[Must-fix] One failed POST hangs the benchmark until the 60-minute timeout**

Each sender goroutine returns after its first `Create` error, but the producer loop keeps writing every remaining item to the unbuffered `work` channel. With the default single sender (or once every sender has failed) nobody reads `work` any more, so `work <- item` blocks forever and the test only ends when `go test -timeout 60m` kills it, without reporting the error that caused it.

**Why:** A reachable failure (any rejected POST) turns into a silent hour-long hang.
**Fix:** Stop producing on the first error: e.g. give the senders a cancellable context (or use errgroup.WithContext) and select on ctx.Done() when sending to work, or have a failing sender keep draining work instead of returning; then report the joined errors.
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: wrong behaviour or missing companion change.

